---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="SA Constitution Privacy Policy - LogicPath Systems">
    <section class="legal-page" style="padding-top: 120px; min-height: 100vh;">
        <div class="container reveal">
            <div class="glass-card" style="padding: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);">
                <header style="margin-bottom: 3rem; text-align: center;">
                    <h1 class="gradient-text">Privacy Policy</h1>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary);"><strong>App:</strong> SA Constitution — Constitution of South Africa</p>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary);"><strong>Last updated:</strong> 11 October 2026</p>
                </header>

                <main class="legal-content">
                    <p><strong>LogicPath Systems</strong> ("we", "our", "us") publishes the <strong>SA Constitution</strong> app — Constitution of South Africa — a free, ad-supported educational app for Android. This policy explains what information is handled when you use it.</p>

                    <h2>1. The short version</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>We do <strong>not</strong> run servers that collect your personal data, and we have no accounts or logins.</li>
                        <li>Your bookmarks, notes and reading progress stay <strong>on your device</strong>.</li>
                        <li>The App shows ads through <strong>Google AdMob</strong> and measures usage with <strong>Google Analytics for Firebase</strong>. These Google services collect device and usage information, described below.</li>
                        <li>Where the law requires it, the App asks for your <strong>consent</strong> before requesting ads, and you can change that choice at any time in the App.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h2>2. Who we are</h2>
                    <p>LogicPath Systems is the developer and data controller for this App.</p>
                    <p>Contact: <a href="mailto:contact@logicpathsystems.com" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);"><strong>contact@logicpathsystems.com</strong></a></p>

                    <h2>3. Information stored on your device only</h2>
                    <p>The App saves the following locally, using your device's app storage:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Bookmarks</strong> — sections you save</li>
                        <li><strong>Personal notes</strong> — your own annotations</li>
                        <li><strong>Reading progress</strong> — sections read, flashcards reviewed, XP, rank, daily streak</li>
                        <li><strong>Recently viewed sections and recent searches</strong></li>
                        <li><strong>Appearance preference</strong> — light, dark or system</li>
                    </ul>
                    <blockquote style="border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-primary); padding-left: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
                        <p>This information is never transmitted to us or to any third party. Removing the App, or clearing its storage, deletes it permanently.</p>
                    </blockquote>

                    <h2>4. Information collected by Google services</h2>
                    <p>The App includes two Google services. They collect information directly from your device. We never receive your name, email address, phone number, contacts, photos or precise GPS location.</p>
                    <div style="overflow-x: auto;">
                        <table style="width: 100%; text-align: left; border-collapse: collapse; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
                            <thead>
                                <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);">
                                    <th style="padding: 0.5rem; color: var(--text-primary);">Service</th>
                                    <th style="padding: 0.5rem; color: var(--text-primary);">What it collects</th>
                                    <th style="padding: 0.5rem; color: var(--text-primary);">Purpose</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);">
                                    <td style="padding: 0.5rem;">Google AdMob</td>
                                    <td style="padding: 0.5rem;">Advertising ID, IP address, approximate (country/city-level) location, device and app information, ad events such as views and clicks</td>
                                    <td style="padding: 0.5rem;">Serving ads, measuring them, limiting repeats, and detecting invalid traffic and fraud</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td style="padding: 0.5rem;">Google Analytics for Firebase</td>
                                    <td style="padding: 0.5rem;">App instance identifier, device model, operating-system version, language, country, app version, and in-app events such as which screens are opened</td>
                                    <td style="padding: 0.5rem;">Understanding how the App is used so we can improve it, and measuring crashes and stability</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    <p>Google processes this information as described in the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">Google Privacy Policy</a> and in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a>.</p>
                    <p>We do <strong>not</strong> send your notes, bookmarks or search text to analytics or to advertisers.</p>

                    <h2>5. Advertising and your consent</h2>
                    <p><strong>Where a consent message applies</strong> (for example the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland), the App shows Google's consent form, built on the IAB Transparency and Consent Framework, <strong>before any ad is requested</strong>. If you do not consent to personalised ads, you may still see non-personalised or limited ads.</p>
                    <p><strong>Changing your mind:</strong> open <strong>My progress → Ad privacy choices</strong> in the App. That entry appears wherever a consent message applies.</p>
                    <p><strong>Android setting:</strong> <strong>Settings → Google → Ads</strong> lets you reset or delete your Advertising ID, or opt out of ad personalisation for every app.</p>
                    <p><strong>Ad formats used:</strong> banner, native, interstitial (between content, at natural pauses) and app-open ads.</p>

                    <h2>6. Legal bases (GDPR / UK GDPR)</h2>
                    <p>Where the GDPR or UK GDPR applies:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Consent</strong> — personalised advertising, and analytics where consent is required. You may withdraw consent at any time, as described above.</li>
                        <li><strong>Legitimate interests</strong> — keeping the App secure, preventing ad fraud, and understanding aggregate usage to improve the App.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h2>7. South African users (POPIA)</h2>
                    <p>For users in South Africa, we process personal information in line with the <strong>Protection of Personal Information Act, 2013 (POPIA)</strong>. You have the right to ask what personal information is held about you, to ask for correction or deletion, and to object to processing. Because we hold no personal information on our own servers, most requests concern information held by Google; section 9 explains how to delete it. You may also lodge a complaint with the Information Regulator of South Africa.</p>

                    <h2>8. Sharing and international transfers</h2>
                    <p>We do not sell your personal information and we do not share it with anyone other than the Google services named above. Google may process and store information on servers outside your country, including in the United States, under its own safeguards for international transfers.</p>

                    <h2>9. Retention and deletion</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>On your device:</strong> delete everything at any time via <strong>Settings → Apps → SA Constitution → Storage → Clear data</strong>, or by uninstalling the App.</li>
                        <li><strong>Advertising data:</strong> reset or delete your Advertising ID in <strong>Settings → Google → Ads</strong>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Analytics data:</strong> retained by Google for a limited period under our Firebase retention setting, then deleted automatically. To request deletion of analytics data linked to your device, contact us with the date and device model and we will ask Google to delete the matching records.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>We keep no user-data backups of our own, because we operate no user-data servers.</p>

                    <h2>10. Children</h2>
                    <p>The App is intended for a general audience — learners, students, legal professionals and members of the public — and is <strong>not directed at children under 13</strong>. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided personal information through the App, contact us and we will act to have it deleted.</p>

                    <h2>11. Security</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Information you create stays in the App's private storage on your device.</li>
                        <li>Data sent to Google AdMob and Firebase is encrypted in transit.</li>
                        <li>The App requests only the Internet permission and the Advertising ID; it does not use the camera, microphone, contacts, or your precise location.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h2>12. Your rights</h2>
                    <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, delete, or restrict the use of your personal information, to object to processing, and to data portability. Write to <a href="mailto:contact@logicpathsystems.com" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);"><strong>contact@logicpathsystems.com</strong></a> and we will respond within the period the law requires. You may also complain to your local data protection authority.</p>

                    <h2>13. Legal content disclaimer</h2>
                    <p>The constitutional text in the App is reproduced from official government publications for educational purposes. The App is <strong>not affiliated with, endorsed by, or representing</strong> the Government of the Republic of South Africa, and nothing in it is legal advice.</p>

                    <h2>14. Changes to this policy</h2>
                    <p>We may update this policy as the App changes. The revised version appears in the App with a new "Last updated" date, and significant changes will be highlighted in the release notes. Continuing to use the App after an update means you accept the revised policy.</p>

                    <h2>15. Contact</h2>
                    <p><strong>LogicPath Systems</strong></p>
                    <p>📧 <a href="mailto:contact@logicpathsystems.com" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);"><strong>contact@logicpathsystems.com</strong></a></p>

                    <p style="margin-top: 2.5rem; color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.95rem;">Effective 11 October 2026. © LogicPath Systems.</p>
                </main>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</Layout>

<style>
    .legal-content h2, .legal-content h3 {
        color: var(--text-primary);
        margin-top: 2.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    .legal-content h2 {
        font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    .legal-content h3 {
        font-size: 1.25rem;
    }
    
    .legal-content p, .legal-content ul, .legal-content table, .legal-content blockquote {
        color: var(--text-secondary);
        margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
        font-size: 1.05rem;
        line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .legal-content ul {
        padding-left: 2rem;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    .legal-content li {
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    .legal-content code {
        background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
        padding: 0.15rem 0.4rem;
        border-radius: 4px;
        font-size: 0.95em;
    }
</style>
